{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["הָעֵז — 'gather in,' as in ״הָעִזוּ בְּנֵי בִנְיָמִין״; ״יֹשְׁבֵי הַגְּבָעוֹת הָעִיזוּ״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Rashbam glosses the rare imperative העז (Exodus 9:19) as 'gather' (cf. BDB), supporting it with two biblical occurrences of the same root. The second quotation is from Jeremiah 6:1; the first, read here as העזו בני בנימין, appears to allude to the same verse (whose MT reads הַזְּיֵנוּ), suggesting Rashbam cites a variant or secondary reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:55.181771548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}